The numbers is a list of 1, 2, 2, and 4.
The count is the number of items in numbers.
The tally is a list of count plus 1 zeros.
For each value in numbers.
Set item value of tally to item value of tally plus 1.

The repeated is 0.
The absent is 0.
For every candidate from 1 to count.
If item candidate of tally is 2, set repeated to candidate.
If item candidate of tally is 0, set absent to candidate.

The report is empty text.
Place format whole number repeated as text into report.
Place "," into report.
Place format whole number absent as text into report.
Show report.
